# Markdown style for news rewrites

Use this file when the user asks for `@markdown-style.mdc`. It is the session house style.

Follow **both**:

1. `.cursor/rules/news-markdown-format.mdc` — compact `titles:` (3), description 140–160, `[tta_listen_btn]`, dateline, proper paragraphs with **no blank lines in the body**, Footer SEO/meta, coverage first, official/celebrity name checks.
2. `.cursor/rules/news-rewriting.mdc` — British English, `US` not `U.S.`, `per cent`, times as `9.00pm`, ordinal dates, no CJK, no outlet attribution, varied paragraph lengths, verify names online.

If the two conflict on skeleton, prefer **news-markdown-format.mdc** (YAML three titles + Footer).
